{#-
  Site footer. Brand + mission on the left, contact on the right; underneath a
  separator, the copyright sits bottom-left and the social links bottom-right.

  The legal-identity block (legal name, org type, V-tal, address + the English
  "official website" sentence) is NOT here — it lives in the "Felagsskapurin"
  panel on /samband/. Google for Nonprofits requires the org's V-tal, a physical
  address, a clear mission and working social links to be openly visible ON THE
  SITE; it does not require them in the footer specifically. The mission and the
  social links stay below, so between this footer and /samband/ the whole
  checklist is still met. Do not drop the /samband/ panel.

  No page-links column: the nav is sticky and always visible.
-#}
<footer class="footer" role="contentinfo">
  <div class="container footer__inner">

    <div class="footer__brand">
      <p class="footer__name">{{ site.name }}</p>
      <p class="footer__mission">{{ site.mission }}</p>
    </div>

    <div class="footer__contact">
      <p class="footer__heading">Samband</p>
      <ul class="footer__links" role="list">
        <li><a href="mailto:{{ site.email }}" class="footer__link">{{ site.email }}</a></li>
        <li><a href="tel:{{ site.phone | replace(' ', '') }}" class="footer__link">{{ site.phone }}</a></li>
      </ul>
    </div>

  </div>

  <div class="footer__bottom">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="footer__copyright">&copy; {% year %} {{ site.legalName }}. Allur rættur tilskilaður.</p>

      <ul class="footer__social" role="list">
        {%- for channel in site.social %}
        <li>
          <a href="{{ channel.url }}" class="footer__social-link"
             target="_blank" rel="noopener">{{ channel.name }}</a>
        </li>
        {%- endfor %}
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</footer>
